# The release zip ships Windows scripts and a Windows text file. cmd.exe is
# the consumer, and an LF-only .bat can break `if (` / `for` blocks. Today
# they read as CRLF only because Git for Windows defaults core.autocrlf=true
# -- a clone that sets it otherwise, or a `git archive` export, gets LF.
# Pin it instead of relying on the cloner's config.
*.bat text eol=crlf
"READ ME FIRST.txt" text eol=crlf
